l-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "New Mexico sits modestly on the Democratic side of the ledger, with a partisan lean of about four points toward Democrats. The presidency is open in 2028, with the incumbent term-limited, so neither party benefits from incumbency. No general-election polls of the state have been published, expert raters have not weighed in, and prediction markets are not yet pricing the race, leaving the state's underlying partisan lean as the main guide.\n\nNeither party's nominee is known, and no fundraising or outside-spending figures exist to sharpen the picture. With only fundamentals to go on, the forecast holds near the state's underlying lean and carries wide uncertainty. A national environment shifting toward either party, or the first polls and ratings pointing a different way, would be the most likely reasons for revision.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6835, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6466, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6493, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6412, "margin": 4.0}]}